 This install applies to "Wing Commander" (c) 1994 Origin.
 Disk versions (SPS #824 and #1657) and the CD32 Dangerous Streets /
 Wing Commander compilation are supported in English and German.
 Wing Commander Enhanced 2.0b (13.11.2026)
 Original install: Psygore. Version 2.0b improvements: Vesuri.

 Requirements:
 -------------
 WHDLoad 17 or newer and xfddecrunch must be available in the command path.
 xfddecrunch is supplied by the XFD package (aminet:util/pack/xfdmaster.lha).
 Use Expert installation mode to select a floppy drive other than DF0:.

 Disk/OCS: 512 KB Chip RAM and 1 MB other RAM, plus about 2.5 MB for PRELOAD.
 CD32/AGA: 640 KB Chip RAM and 1.4 MB other RAM, plus about 4.1 MB for PRELOAD.
 Additional free memory is needed for WHDLoad and the enhanced renderer.
 For enhanced play, use a 68020 or better with Fast RAM. The tested OCS
 configuration starts at 512 KB Chip RAM and 4 MB Fast RAM including PRELOAD.
 Rendering speed depends on the processor and scene; 50 FPS is not guaranteed.

 The OCS slave requires an A500 Kickstart 1.3 image:
   Devs:Kickstarts/kick34005.A500
   Devs:Kickstarts/kick34005.A500.RTB
 The CD32 slave requires an A1200 or A4000 Kickstart 3.1 image:
   Devs:Kickstarts/kick40068.A1200 and kick40068.A1200.RTB, or
   Devs:Kickstarts/kick40068.A4000 and kick40068.A4000.RTB
 Supply your own ROM image, extracted using GrabKick or a similar tool.
 The matching RTB files are available in aminet:util/boot/skick346.lha.
 WHDLoad rejects an incorrect or altered ROM image.

 Installation:
 -------------
 Run Install and select the disk or CD32 edition. The disk installer requests
 WingDisk1, WingDisk2 and WingDisk3, identifies English/German, and unpacks the
 executable. The CD32 installer copies Wingco from the disc named Bundle: and
 unpacks both language executables. Keep the two editions in separate drawers.
 Existing destination drawers are preserved; choose a new destination instead.
 Manual and QuickDocEN/DE/FR/IT are included, together with the original icons.

 Features and options:
 ---------------------
 Quit with '*' (PrtSc), or select another key using WHDLoad's QUITKEY tooltype.
 A mouse in port 0 moves the pointer in the rooms and menus, in every mode.
 Its left button works as fire: it clicks, skips and continues sequences, and
 fires the guns in flight. The joystick, CD32 pad and keys work as before.
 The installed icon enables enhanced mode and DCACHE by default. NOCACHE can
 be used to disable caching. Enhancements currently support English only;
 German uses original behaviour. Enhanced OCS supports SPS #1657 only.

 CUSTOM1: 0 = English, 1 = German.
 CUSTOM2: 0 = cheats off, 1 = cheat mode, 2 = invincible cheat mode.
 In cheat mode hold SHIFT and press:
   F1  music on/off                 F6  self-destruct
   F2  sound effects on/off         F7  cockpit damage graphics
   F3  video images on/off          F8  game information
   F4  message speed                F9  pause for screenshots
   F5  destroy locked target        F10 eject
 CUSTOM3 selects a system (cheat mode required):
   0 Default       1 Enyo          2 McAuliffe       3 Gateway
   4 Gimle         5 Brimstone     6 Chengdu         7 Dakota
   8 Port Hedland  9 Kurasawa     10 Rostov         11 Hubble's Star
  12 Venice       13 Hell's Kitchen
 CUSTOM4: 0 = mission 1, 1 = mission 2, 2 = mission 3 (cheat mode required).

 OCS CUSTOM5:
   1 = Enhanced framerate (68020+Fast RAM), enabled in the installed icon.
   0 or unset = original timing and rendering.
 A 68000/68010 or a machine without suitable Fast RAM always uses original
 behaviour, regardless of this option. Slow expansion RAM does not qualify.

 CD32 CUSTOM5:
   0 or unset = Enhanced (English); German uses Psygore normal.
   1 = Psygore normal        2 = Psygore unlimited
   3 = Psygore relaxed       4 = Psygore slow
 Original simulation and rendering remain available with modes 1-4.
 When updating an old icon, note that the 1.0 modes 0-3 are now numbered 1-4.
 The old CUSTOM5=4 original-conversion option has been removed.

 History:
 --------
 Version 2.0b (13.11.2026) by Vesuri:
 - Optional enhanced framerate with smoother flight, cameras and ship effects.
 - Consistent game speed on faster processors and smoother cinematic movement.
 - Retimed intro, room, briefing, launch, landing, death and funeral animations.
 - Improved projectile appearance and asteroid/mine hit detection.
 - Waypoint markers stay visible in front of nebulae in every English mode.
 - More responsive room controls with limited cursor speed.
 - CD32 edition: a saved pilot appears in the bunk at once, not only after the
   next reload.
 - Choosing a Training Simulator opponent with keys 1-4 shows the right ship.
 - Mouse control of the room and menu pointer; the left mouse button works as
   fire. The first click after entering a screen is no longer ignored.
 - Disk edition: faster arithmetic and collision checks in every mode, including
   the Amiga 500, without changing game behaviour.
 - Enhanced mode and caches enabled in newly installed icons; original modes
   remain available.

Version 1.0 (11.01.2014) by Psygore:
 - Nice color/newicon (created by Frank/Dr.Zarkov) and BoxIcon included
 - Some accesses fault patched
 - CD32 hardware chunky to planar (AKIKO chipset) replaced by software
 - Bugs in music replay routine fixed (thanks to Don Adan for the info)
 - Lowlevel and nonvolatile libraries functions patched
 - Manual and quick doc included
 - Quit with '*' (PrtSc)

